WEBVTT

00:22:29.997 --> 00:22:32.287
she was helping kids
get out of elementary school

00:22:32.311 --> 00:22:34.804
and walk across the street,
sort of a crossing guard.

00:22:34.828 --> 00:22:37.491
He said, "Are you being paid?"
"No, I'm not being paid."

00:22:37.515 --> 00:22:39.491
He said, "What are you doing after this?"

00:22:39.515 --> 00:22:41.879
"Taking food to the hospital
for the sick people."

00:22:41.903 --> 00:22:44.001
He said, "Do you have
any time to volunteer?"

00:22:44.025 --> 00:22:46.228
She said, "No, I don't
have time to volunteer!"

00:22:46.252 --> 00:22:48.260
And she didn't regard that
as volunteering.

00:22:48.284 --> 00:22:49.718
That's just what neighbors do.

00:22:49.742 --> 00:22:52.370
And I think one of the problems
we've had in our country

00:22:52.394 --> 00:22:54.158
is we've lost the art of neighboring,

00:22:54.182 --> 00:22:57.689
and there are a certain set of skills
and norms that neighboring involves.

00:22:57.713 --> 00:23:00.390
Transitions: when somebody moves in,
you welcome them in.